From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kirill <sleeply4cat@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:57:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/23] clk: qcom: alpha-pll: honour FSM legacy mode on Trion
 and Lucid PLLs

clk_trion_pll_configure() ignores SUPPORTS_FSM_LEGACY_MODE, which the
Alpha configure path honours and downstream sets here too. Without the
bit gpll10 on SM6225 never locks, so nothing clocked from it can start.
SM6375 carries the same flag and also changes behaviour here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015ya7ekTBjucpaN4ypc4DaZ
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c
index 4adb1344d..b1ba0fb25 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c
@@ -1749,6 +1749,10 @@ void clk_trion_pll_configure(struct clk_alpha_pll *pll, struct regmap *regmap,
 	regmap_update_bits(regmap, PLL_MODE(pll), PLL_UPDATE_BYPASS,
 			   PLL_UPDATE_BYPASS);
 
+	if (pll->flags & SUPPORTS_FSM_LEGACY_MODE)
+		regmap_update_bits(regmap, PLL_MODE(pll), PLL_FSM_LEGACY_MODE,
+				   PLL_FSM_LEGACY_MODE);
+
 	/* Disable PLL output */
 	regmap_update_bits(regmap, PLL_MODE(pll),  PLL_OUTCTRL, 0);
 
